From: Anton Argirov <anton.argirov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:00:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cocoa): present frames asynchronously with Core Animation

OpenGL presentation can stall for several frame periods even when
emulation runs at 50 Hz. Keep one frame pending on the main thread and
hand it to Core Animation as an immutable image. This removes the wait
in glFlush from the window thread and avoids reusing image data while
the compositor still owns it.

